\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/reliable-sources-for-wikipedia\",\"description\":\"A clear guide to reliable, independent sources on Wikipedia, including what usually works, what to avoid, and how to evaluate coverage quality.\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":5,\"name\":\"How to Get Your Business on Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-to-get-your-business-on-wikipedia\",\"description\":\"A realistic guide to getting a business represented on Wikipedia, including eligibility, source requirements, neutral writing, and responsible next steps.\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":6,\"name\":\"Wikipedia Article Guidelines for Businesses\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/wikipedia-article-guidelines-for-businesses\",\"description\":\"Key Wikipedia guidelines businesses should understand before creating or editing an article, including notability, neutrality, sourcing, and disclosure.\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":7,\"name\":\"Wikipedia Conflict of Interest Policy Explained\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/wikipedia-conflict-of-interest-policy-explained\",\"description\":\"Understand Wikipedia conflict-of-interest and paid-contribution expectations, and how connected editors can participate more responsibly.\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":8,\"name\":\"How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles\",\"description\":\"Learn how Wikipedia editors evaluate new and existing articles, including sourcing, notability, neutrality, and policy compliance.\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":9,\"name\":\"Wikipedia Page vs Company Website\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/wikipedia-page-vs-company-website\",\"description\":\"Compare a Wikipedia page and a company website: purpose, control, tone, sourcing, and when each is appropriate for a business.\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":10,\"name\":\"Common Wikipedia Submission Mistakes\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/common-wikipedia-submission-mistakes\",\"description\":\"Avoid common mistakes when preparing a Wikipedia article, from weak sources and promotional tone to conflict-of-interest and notability errors.\"}]}</script><section class=\"hero-grid text-white\"><div class=\"grid-lines\"><div class=\"container-tight py-20 md:py-24\"><p class=\"mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-electric\"><span class=\"text-sky-300\">Insights &amp; Resources</span></p><h1 class=\"font-display max-w-4xl text-4xl font-semibold md:text-5xl\">Wikipedia guides, tips, and editorial resources</h1><p class=\"mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/78\">Practical, policy-aware resources on Wikipedia page creation, notability, reliable sources, and responsible article preparation. These guides are informational and do not guarantee Wikipedia publication or retention.</p></div></div></section><section class=\"section-pad \"><div class=\"container-tight grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3\"><article class=\"flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-border bg-white p-6 shadow-sm\"><p class=\"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-electric\">Wikipedia</p><h2 class=\"mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-navy\"><a class=\"hover:text-electric\" href=\"/blog/how-to-create-a-wikipedia-page-for-your-company\">How to Create a Wikipedia Page for Your Company</a></h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-xs font-medium text-muted\">Published <!-- -->2026-11-10</p><p class=\"mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted\">A practical guide to evaluating eligibility, gathering independent reliable sources, and following Wikipedia’s policies before creating a company article.</p><a class=\"mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-navy\" href=\"/blog/how-to-create-a-wikipedia-page-for-your-company\">Read guide <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" str